Mr. Marchwood-Reyes,<br />
<br />
Following your question at last week's industry panel, and without turning =
this into guidance the staff has not issued.<br />
<br />
The amendments to Form PF adopted in 2023 add current reporting for certain=
 events at private equity and hedge fund advisers, expand the reporting on =
master-feeder and parallel structures, and change how you report the fund's=
 investments. Compliance dates differ by section, and the current reporting=
 obligations came in first. Marchwood Capital reports annually, which does =
not exempt you from the current reporting requirements that apply to your f=
und types.<br />
<br />
The practical point is that the current reporting clock runs in business da=
ys from the event, not from the quarter end, so the firm needs a process th=
at identifies a triggering event when it happens rather than a process that=
 looks for them at reporting time. Advisers that discover the event during =
their normal quarterly close are already late.<br />
<br />
Read the adopting release rather than a summary of it. If after that you ha=
ve a structural question about the master and its feeders, send it to me in=
 writing.<br />
